From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sf2000 linux port <sf2000@local>
Date: Wed, 13 May 2026 05:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mips: sf2000: prefer explicit bFLT HI16 reloc state

Some MIPS code has unrelated LUI instructions using the same register
between a HI16 relocation and a later LO16 relocation. One observed
BusyBox sequence loads h_errno into v1, then has a LO16 relocation for
__searchdomain that pairs with an earlier explicit HI16 relocation, not
with the nearer h_errno LUI.

Prefer the most recently processed explicit HI16 relocation when its
target register matches the LO16 instruction. Keep the instruction scan
as a fallback for LO16 relocations whose HI16 was not present in the
linear relocation stream.
---
 arch/mips/include/asm/flat.h | 12 ++++++------
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/mips/include/asm/flat.h b/arch/mips/include/asm/flat.h
--- a/arch/mips/include/asm/flat.h
+++ b/arch/mips/include/asm/flat.h
@@ -83,6 +83,12 @@ static inline int flat_mips_find_hi16_for_lo16(u32 __user *rp, u32 lo,
 	u32 rs = flat_mips_lo16_rs(lo);
 	int i;
 
+	if (flat_mips_hi16_rp && flat_mips_lui_rt(flat_mips_hi16_insn) == rs) {
+		*hi_rp = flat_mips_hi16_rp;
+		*hi_insn = flat_mips_hi16_insn;
+		return 1;
+	}
+
 	for (i = 1; i <= FLAT_MIPS_HI16_SCAN; i++) {
 		u32 *scan = p - i;
 		u32 insn = get_unaligned(scan);
@@ -101,12 +107,6 @@ static inline int flat_mips_find_hi16_for_lo16(u32 __user *rp, u32 lo,
 		return 1;
 	}
 
-	if (flat_mips_hi16_rp && flat_mips_lui_rt(flat_mips_hi16_insn) == rs) {
-		*hi_rp = flat_mips_hi16_rp;
-		*hi_insn = flat_mips_hi16_insn;
-		return 1;
-	}
-
 	*hi_rp = NULL;
 	*hi_insn = 0;
 	return 0;
-- 
2.49.0
